{
  "status": "verified fixed-quality ribbon sampling regression; full Phase 3.1 remains open",
  "owner": "Phase 3.1",
  "source_before": "70ca9c49f454728da618dd00298369aba052b8e1",
  "implementation": [
    "Shared ribbon preparation uses the resolved quality tier once and never reduces its sampling limit to fit an arbitrary 400000-vertex threshold.",
    "Removed the size-dependent retry loop, reduction helper and four tests that codified quality loss. One observable large-source regression replaces them.",
    "A source of 9000 C-alpha guides requires 26111040 bytes of ribbon vertices at the requested eight-step limit. The old path uploaded only 10753088 bytes. The new path uploads the exact full-quality geometry.",
    "A renderer with a 16 MiB storage limit returns the typed LimitExceeded error for cartoon vertices instead of silently lowering fidelity. Existing bounded GPU allocation checks own the failure.",
    "The MolStar B-tube-1AON reference now uses the actual polymer-tube visual through putty with uniform radius 0.3, eight linear segments and sixteen radial segments. The former cartoon adapter enabled tubular helices, a different presentation. Reference source was inspected; no implementation code was copied."
  ],
  "public_surfaces": "Rust, command, Python and WASM specifications are unchanged. Their existing quality requests now govern large ribbons without a hidden secondary reduction. Actual Python/Chromium consumers render 1AON and 1BNA using three profile variants; Python resolves exact visible opaque picks.",
  "complexity": "One O(guides + samples) geometry preparation replaces repeated rebuilding with smaller sample limits. Full-fidelity device geometry can consume more memory and render time. Camera-only cache reuse and the source coordinate seam remain unchanged.",
  "regression": {
    "test": "engine::ribbon_quality_tests::a_large_fixed_quality_ribbon_keeps_every_requested_sample",
